cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "Proteus: a headless port schedule labelled by a reduced C. elegans connectome readout"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic C99 simulator of a 279-neuron C. elegans connectome
  (graded potentials, short-term synaptic plasticity, neuromodulators)
  supplies a reduced six-scalar readout that labels a headless TCP port
  schedule in bio mode. The move tick is set by the body speed reflex and
  the detector, not by the connectome, so the artifact does not establish a
  closed loop. The release ships preregistered hypotheses, falsification
  criteria and negative results alongside the code.
authors:
